-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore).  SEAT TESTS: one case at least per question, and a case where the Act does not answer.
-- Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion, before running.  Inputs are given in the order of the question's GIVEN lines.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`
IMPORT `soga-part4-performance`
IMPORT `soga-part7-supplementary`
IMPORT `soga-seat`

-- Does the Act apply to my contract, and in what words? (s 1)
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` (Date 31 12 1893) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` (Date 1 1 1894) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my contract` (Date 15 6 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Schedule change a section for my contract` (Date 1 6 2024) `section 14` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Schedule change a section for my contract` (Date 1 6 1980) `section 14` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Schedule change a section for my contract` (Date 1 6 1950) `section 55` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Schedule change a section for my contract` (Date 1 6 1980) `section 55` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Schedule change a section for my contract` (Date 31 12 1893) `section 14` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Schedule change a section for my contract` (Date 1 6 1980) `a section with no reference to the Schedule` EQUALS NOTHING

